# Flask Backend Rules

## App structure

Use an application factory and blueprints — not a single 500-line `main.py`.

```
backend/
  app/
    __init__.py      # create_app()
    models/          # SQLAlchemy models
    routes/          # Blueprints (e.g. todos.py)
    schemas/         # Request/response validation (optional)
  config.py
  wsgi.py            # entry point for production
```

```python
# ✅ GOOD — factory pattern
def create_app(config=None):
    app = Flask(__name__)
    app.config.from_object(config or "config.DevelopmentConfig")
    db.init_app(app)
    app.register_blueprint(todos_bp, url_prefix="/api/todos")
    return app
```

## Routes and responses

- REST-ish URLs: `GET /api/todos`, `POST /api/todos`, `PATCH /api/todos/<id>`.
- Always return JSON with correct status codes.

```python
# ❌ BAD
@app.route("/todo")
def todo():
    return str(todo_list)  # not JSON, wrong type

# ✅ GOOD
@todos_bp.get("/")
def list_todos():
    todos = Todo.query.order_by(Todo.created_at.desc()).all()
    return jsonify([t.to_dict() for t in todos]), 200
```

| Action | Status |
|--------|--------|
| GET success | 200 |
| POST created | 201 |
| PATCH success | 200 |
| DELETE success | 204 (no body) |
| Not found | 404 |
| Validation error | 400 |
| Server error | 500 |

## Request validation

- Read JSON with `request.get_json(silent=True)` and validate before touching the DB.
- Reject missing or empty `title` on create/update.

```python
# ✅ GOOD
data = request.get_json(silent=True) or {}
title = (data.get("title") or "").strip()
if not title:
    return jsonify({"error": "title is required"}), 400
```

## Database access in routes

- Keep routes thin: validate → call model/service → return JSON.
- Do not run raw SQL strings; use the ORM (see database rules).

## CORS

- `flask-cors` is installed — restrict origins in production, allow Vite dev server locally (`http://localhost:5173`).

## Error handling

```python
# ✅ Register handlers in create_app()
@app.errorhandler(404)
def not_found(e):
    return jsonify({"error": "not found"}), 404
```

- Log unexpected exceptions; never expose stack traces to clients in production.

## Bad habits to avoid

- Putting business logic directly in route handlers without models/services.
- Using global mutable lists/dicts as a "database" — use SQLAlchemy.
- `@app.route` for everything in one file — use blueprints.
- Returning HTML from API routes.
- Running with `debug=True` in production.
